    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113">

                <pb facs="0250" n="138" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg138"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-05T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 5, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>British Government informs Department through Embassy at London that latest
                    advices from Peking indicate that “Japanese <pb facs="0251" n="139"
                        xml:id="pg139"/> group has decided to defer making proposed advance on
                    account of uncertainty of political situation in China and until a stable
                    government is in sight.” Telegraph whether this report is correct.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
